<LegalPage
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="Terms for using the NW Drone & Media website and booking filming, photography and drone services."
  updated={LEGAL_UPDATED}
  intro="The ground rules for using this site and booking our services."
>
  <p>
    These terms cover your use of this website and the general terms for services provided by {SITE.name}. Each booked
    project is also covered by its own signed agreement; if the two conflict, the signed agreement wins.
  </p>

  <h2>Using this website</h2>
  <p>
    Content on this site, including photos, video, text and design, belongs to {SITE.name} or is used with permission. You may
    view and share links to it, but you may not copy, download or reuse it without written permission.
  </p>
  <p>
    Prices, packages and availability shown on the site are for general information and may change. A quote or signed
    agreement is the only binding statement of price and scope.
  </p>

  <h2>Bookings and payment</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A date is reserved once the agreement is signed and the retainer is paid.</li>
    <li>Payment schedules, cancellation and rescheduling terms are set out in each project agreement.</li>
    <li>Travel fees may apply outside our standard service area.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Drone operations</h2>
  <p>
    All flights are conducted under FAA Part 107 and are subject to airspace authorization, weather and site conditions. The
    remote pilot in command has final say on whether, where and when it is safe and legal to fly. See our
    <a href="/flight-safety/">Flight Safety &amp; FAA Compliance</a> page for details.
  </p>

  <h2>Deliverables and usage rights</h2>
  <p>
    We retain copyright in all footage and images we create. Clients receive a license to use their deliverables for the
    purposes described in their agreement (for example, personal use for wedding films or marketing use for commercial
    projects). We may use selected work in our portfolio unless the client opts out in writing.
  </p>

  <h2>Client responsibilities</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Provide accurate dates, locations and timelines.</li>
    <li>Obtain any venue or property-owner permission needed for filming and takeoff/landing.</li>
    <li>Tell us about known hazards, restrictions or sensitive areas at the site.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent allowed by law, our total liability for any claim related to a project is limited to the amount paid for
    that project. We are not liable for indirect or consequential losses, or for coverage missed because of weather, airspace
    restrictions, venue rules or other circumstances outside our control.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Washington.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p>
</LegalPage>
